# SURAKSHA — optional environment variables.
#
# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and restart the dev server: Vite freezes env values
# into the bundle at build time, so hot reload will NOT pick up an edit.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   npm run maps:check     # tells you if the key is actually readable
#
# Only names starting with VITE_ reach browser code. Without these keys SURAKSHA
# uses its built-in simulated map and local demo auth — nothing else breaks.

# Google Maps JavaScript API key (39 chars, starts with "AIza").
# Enable "Maps JavaScript API" in the same Cloud project.
# On Vercel, set the same name (or GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY) in Project Settings.
# The site reads it live from /api/maps-config, so saving the variable is
# enough — it does not have to have been present when Vite last built.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional: a Maps JavaScript API "Map ID" (map_ids=…). Only needed for vector
# maps or AdvancedMarkerElement; the app works without it.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase Auth (optional)
#
# Leave both blank for the built-in local demo auth (signs in on-device).
# To route sign-in through Supabase Auth, paste your project's PUBLIC values:
#
#   1. In the Supabase dashboard: Project Settings → API
#   2. Copy "Project URL" and the "anon" / "public" key (NEVER service_role).
#
# The anon key is designed to be public — it gates access via Row Level
# Security policies, not secrecy.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...
